{
  "id": "colinhacks_zod_6267",
  "repo_name": "colinhacks/zod",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/colinhacks/zod",
  "base_commit": "53cec2a0d0941a69d8add934ac3a8695fb5fb14c",
  "pr_number": 6267,
  "issue_number": 6104,
  "issue_title": "Expose ZodFunction schema from .implement() result",
  "issue_body": "Zod 4 function schemas are close to ideal for introspectable function definitions:\n\n```ts\nexport const install = z.function()\n  .input(z.tuple([z.string().describe('package name')]))\n  .implement(pkg => ({installed: pkg, success: true}))\n```\n\nBut not ideal, because we can't get the `input` schema back out of the above anywhere.\n\nUse case: [`trpc-cli`](https://github.com/mmkal/trpc-cli) can turn a plain module of exported functions into CLI commands. Right now it only supports a vendored/patched `typebox` which can read plain-typescript types (so `export function install(name: string) {return {...}}` works roughly like the above.\n\nIt'd be great for advanced use cases to use `z.function` like the above, since parsing typescript types doesn't allow for runtime transforms/custom metadata etc. It can't work now because the input schema is lost.\n\nI read you saying before that most proposed uses around `z.function()` as a schema are anti-patterns. I think this one is narrower:\n\n- no additional validation steps\n- not asking to restore v3 `z.function()` semantics\n- just asking to expose an already-tracked-internally schema as a gettable property\n\n## Current behavior\n\n`ZodFunction` has schema:\n\n```ts\nconst Fn = z.function().input(...)\nFn._def.input // usable at runtime, albeit internal\n\nconst fn = Fn.implement(pkg => ({installed: pkg, success: true}))\n\nfn._def // undefined\nfn._zod // undefined\nObject.getOwnPropertySymbols(fn) // []\n```\n\nIt could be non-enumerable, maybe symbol-keyed, read-only. Could return `undefined` for non-Zod fns.\n\nTyping could be:\n\n```ts\ntype ImplementedZodFunction<T extends z.ZodFunction> = T['_input'] & {\n  _zod: T\n}\n```\n\n## Related\n\n- #4143: Zod 4 `z.function()` replacement / anti-pattern discussion\n- #4842: extracting fn signature from Zod function schema\n- #5121: `z.function()` extends `$ZodType`\n- #313: older request for lighter function syntax; Zod 4 mostly solved syntax side\n\n## Implementation\n\nHopefully `issue` is more valuable than `pull request` these days, but I did an implementation just to double-check that it is indeed easy and confirm that the maintenance burden would be near zero. Here's the full implementation diff. I'd be happy to open a PR and add tests + brief docs if ur ok with this:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/packages/zod/src/v4/core/schemas.ts b/packages/zod/src/v4/core/schemas.ts\nindex 4f85fbf0..2c414284 100644\n--- a/packages/zod/src/v4/core/schemas.ts\n+++ b/packages/zod/src/v4/core/schemas.ts\n@@ -4397,13 +4397,17 @@ export interface $ZodFunction<\n   implement<F extends $InferInnerFunctionType<Args, Returns>>(\n     func: F\n   ): // allow for return type inference\n-  (\n+  ((\n     ...args: Parameters<this[\"_output\"]>\n-  ) => ReturnType<F> extends ReturnType<this[\"_output\"]> ? ReturnType<F> : ReturnType<this[\"_output\"]>;\n+  ) => ReturnType<F> extends ReturnType<this[\"_output\"]> ? ReturnType<F> : ReturnType<this[\"_output\"]>) & {\n+    _zod: $ZodFunctionInternals<Args, Returns>;\n+  };\n \n   implementAsync<F extends $InferInnerFunctionTypeAsync<Args, Returns>>(\n     func: F\n-  ): F extends $InferOuterFunctionTypeAsync<Args, Returns> ? F : $InferOuterFunctionTypeAsync<Args, Returns>;\n+  ): (F extends $InferOuterFunctionTypeAsync<Args, Returns> ? F : $InferOuterFunctionTypeAsync<Args, Returns>) & {\n+    _zod: $ZodFunctionInternals<Args, Returns>;\n+  };\n \n   input<const Items extends util.TupleItems, const Rest extends $ZodFunctionOut = $ZodFunctionOut>(\n     args: Items,\n@@ -4431,7 +4435,7 @@ export const $ZodFunction: core.$constructor<$ZodFunction> = /*@__PURE__*/ core.\n       if (typeof func !== \"function\") {\n         throw new Error(\"implement() must be called with a function\");\n       }\n-      return function (this: any, ...args: never[]) {\n+      const implemented = function (this: any, ...args: never[]) {\n         const parsedArgs = inst._def.input ? parse(inst._def.input, args) : args;\n         const result = Reflect.apply(func, this, parsedArgs as never[]);\n         if (inst._def.output) {\n@@ -4439,20 +4443,30 @@ export const $ZodFunction: core.$constructor<$ZodFunction> = /*@__PURE__*/ core.\n         }\n         return result as any;\n       };\n+      Object.defineProperty(implemented, \"_zod\", {\n+        value: inst._zod,\n+        enumerable: false,\n+      });\n+      return implemented as any;\n     };\n \n     inst.implementAsync = (func) => {\n       if (typeof func !== \"function\") {\n         throw new Error(\"implementAsync() must be called with a function\");\n       }\n-      return async function (this: any, ...args: never[]) {\n+      const implemented = async function (this: any, ...args: never[]) {\n         const parsedArgs = inst._def.input ? await parseAsync(inst._def.input, args) : args;\n         const result = await Reflect.apply(func, this, parsedArgs as never[]);\n         if (inst._def.output) {\n           return await parseAsync(inst._def.output, result);\n         }\n         return result;\n-      } as any;\n+      };\n+      Object.defineProperty(implemented, \"_zod\", {\n+        value: inst._zod,\n+        enumerable: false,\n+      });\n+      return implemented as any;\n     };\n \n     inst._zod.parse = (payload, _ctx) => {\n\n```",
